   "about": "Assesses Japan’s wartime industrial capacity, labor supply, administration, strategic choices, and dependence on resources within its Inner Zone.",
   "summary": "The surviving portion begins with constraints on cutting tools, bearings, and skilled personnel, then estimates aircraft, vehicle, and ordnance production. It examines manpower transfers and Tojo’s efforts to centralize control of key industries. Later chapters assess possible offensives and argue that Japan is strengthening a northern Inner Zone comprising Japan Proper and nearby continental territories. Tables and appended charts map production, regional resources, stockpiles, and vulnerabilities; the report concludes that control of Manchuria and Korea is central to Japan’s war economy.",
